  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c911ebf07650941888581c84899f6317, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questions:
  - description: In a tug-of-war, if both teams pull equally, the rope stays in place.
      What does this show?
    trueAnswer: Balanced Forces
    answers:
    - Balanced Forces
    - Unbalanced forces
    - Rope is too heavy
    - No forces
  - description: "You push a classroom wall but it doesn\u2019t move. What\u2019s
      happening?"
    trueAnswer: The wall pushes back equally
    answers:
    - The wall pushes back equally
    - Gravity cancels it
    - "You\u2019re too weak"
    - No force was applied
  - description: A student walks 20 m east to the canteen, then 20 m back to class.
      What is the displacement?
    trueAnswer: 0 m
    answers:
    - 0 m
    - 20 m
    - 40 m
    - 60 m
  - description: You drop a crumpled paper and a flat sheet. Why does the flat one
      fall slower?
    trueAnswer: Gravity and air resistance
    answers:
    - Only gravity pulls
    - Gravity and air resistance
    - No forces
    - The paper is lazy
  - description: You and two friends push a stalled tricycle. It finally starts moving
      forward. Why?
    trueAnswer: Unbalanced forces
    answers:
    - No force was applied
    - Balanced forces
    - Unbalanced forces
    - It sticks to the wall
  - description: When does the force of gravity exist?
    trueAnswer: Apply strength
    answers:
    - Apply strength
    - Apply telekinesis
    - Apply black magic
    - Apply force
  - description: "A box rests on the floor. Why doesn\u2019t it fall through?"
    trueAnswer: Gravity disappears
    answers:
    - No force acts
    - The floor pushes up as hard as gravity pulls
    - Gravity disappears
    - The box floats
  - description: Your fitness tracker says you walked 5 km today, but your displacement
      is only 500 m. Why?
    trueAnswer: Displacement = straight-line change
    answers:
    - Displacement = straight-line change
    - Distance and displacement are the same
    - Tracker is broken
    - No forces acted
  - description: Which describes distance and not displacement?
    trueAnswer: "It\u2019s total path traveled"
    answers:
    - It has direction
    - "It\u2019s total path traveled"
    - "It\u2019s straight-line"
    - It can be negative
  - description: A student runs 200 m in 40 seconds. What is their average speed?
    trueAnswer: 5 m/s
    answers:
    - 2 m/s
    - 4 m/s
    - 5 m/s
    - 8 m/s
